<figure class="fte-diagram" data-diagram-id="service-research-foresight-frontier-path" aria-labelledby="fte-title" aria-describedby="fte-caption fte-note">
  <div class="fte-header">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow text-cobalt">Route artifact · research and foresight</p>
      <h2 id="fte-title" class="mt-5 max-w-3xl font-display text-3xl font-medium tracking-[-0.05em] md:text-4xl">Move a frontier signal through a decision path.</h2>
      <p id="fte-caption" class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">Research earns its place when a leader can see what is known, what is uncertain, which assumption matters, and what low-regret experiment should run next. The path separates sensing from committing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="fte-stamp" aria-hidden="true"><span>F → E</span><small>READINESS PATH</small></div>
  </div>

  <div class="fte-visual" role="img" aria-label="A six-stage path from scan through decision, with uncertainty narrowing as evidence and readiness increase." tabindex="0">
    <div class="fte-axis"><span>uncertainty</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i><span>decision confidence</span></div>
    <ol class="fte-path" aria-hidden="true">
      <li><span>Signal</span><strong>Scan</strong><small>horizon</small></li>
      <li><span>Question</span><strong>Frame</strong><small>boundary</small></li>
      <li><span>Evidence</span><strong>Test</strong><small>assumption</small></li>
      <li><span>Scenario</span><strong>Model</strong><small>implication</small></li>
      <li><span>Readiness</span><strong>Prepare</strong><small>capability</small></li>
      <li><span>Option</span><strong>Decide</strong><small>commitment</small></li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <ol class="fte-stages" aria-label="Six stages from frontier research to enterprise decision" tabindex="0">
    <li><span class="fte-number">Scan</span><h3>Collect the signal.</h3><p>Track research, market, policy, competitor, and technical shifts without treating novelty as proof.</p><strong>Artifact · signal ledger</strong></li>
    <li><span class="fte-number">Frame</span><h3>Ask the consequential question.</h3><p>Connect the signal to a decision, exposure, time horizon, and stakeholder who can act.</p><strong>Artifact · inquiry brief</strong></li>
    <li><span class="fte-number">Test</span><h3>Buy information cheaply.</h3><p>Use a bounded experiment, benchmark, or expert review to challenge the assumption carrying the most risk.</p><strong>Artifact · evidence memo</strong></li>
    <li><span class="fte-number">Model</span><h3>Make scenarios comparable.</h3><p>Describe plausible futures, leading indicators, constraints, and the choices that remain reversible.</p><strong>Artifact · scenario register</strong></li>
    <li><span class="fte-number">Prepare</span><h3>Build readiness before urgency.</h3><p>For quantum or other frontier shifts, identify data, skills, interfaces, suppliers, security, and governance dependencies.</p><strong>Artifact · readiness backlog</strong></li>
    <li><span class="fte-number">Decide</span><h3>Commit to a next move.</h3><p>Choose the option, trigger, owner, and review date; keep the evidence path open for the next update.</p><strong>Artifact · decision record</strong></li>
  </ol>

  <div class="fte-footer">
    <p id="fte-note"><strong>Accessible reading:</strong> the stage sequence are the authoritative path. The diagonal line is a visual metaphor for uncertainty becoming more useful—not a forecast.</p>
    <p class="fte-legend"><span><i class="is-cobalt"></i>research</span><span><i class="is-accent"></i>readiness</span><span><i class="is-ink"></i>decision</span></p>
  </div>
</figure>

